# Evidence and reasoning invariants

Preserve:

- Change Intent ≠ Deployment ≠ realized Change;
- anticipated effect ≠ normative Expectation;
- Deployment attempt ≠ activation;
- activation ≠ intended effect realized;
- expectation ≠ baseline;
- planned value ≠ empirical baseline;
- observation ≠ assessment;
- missing evidence ≠ observed absence;
- typical ≠ healthy;
- atypical ≠ degraded/defective;
- successful execution ≠ freshness ≠ data quality;
- planned topology ≠ active Lineage;
- Lineage/reachability ≠ cause/confirmed impact;
- Change ≠ degradation ≠ cause;
- effective/event time ≠ recorded/knowledge time;
- correlation ≠ attribution ≠ confirmed cause.

Rules:

- Time/history is first-class and must support ledger-like append/supersede/correction semantics.
- Material conclusions remain traceable to provenance-bearing evidence.
- A Change Intent may register a prospective Baseline comparability break but cannot set post-change Baseline values.
- Post-change Baseline requires sufficient comparable post-change Observations.
- Planned anticipated behavior becomes normative only through explicit Expectation establishment/revision.
- Missing telemetry never becomes zero/no-event.
- Assessments retain exact Observation and Expectation/Baseline versions/basis.
- Health dimensions stay separate unless an explicit aggregation rule exists.
- Lineage is typed, temporal, historical, authorization-aware, and graph-compatible.
- Do not select graph database, event store, blockchain, or persistence architecture during Phase 002.
- Never infer cause from Deployment timing, Lineage, realized Change, or intent consistency alone.
- Business-facing explanations and engineering detail derive from the same authorized history/evidence.
